    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d456">

                <pb facs="0618" n="519" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg519"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.6552/7: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Third Secretary of Embassy in Spain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wendelin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-09-01T11:00:00+00:00">September 1, 1936—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 1—10:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>X–116. Italian Embassy will leave Madrid for Alicante tonight, so informed
                    Spanish Government last night and requests us not to make this public until
                    their departure. Departure of German<anchor n="63" xml:id="d456-f1"/> and
                    Italian Embassies and arrival of Russian Ambassador are clearly for political
                    reasons and may herald important international developments. Russian Ambassador
                    presented letters of credence to President of Spanish Republic August 29.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wendelin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d456-f1" n="63" xml:id="d456-f1-content">
                <p>The German Chargé and staff left Madrid by plane for Alicante on August 30
                    (701.6252/16).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
